    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33110" root="فحث" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحِثٌ</span></b>  (S, O, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحِثَةٌ</span></b>  (TA) The [<i>portion,</i> or <i>appertenance, called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَفِث</span> (S, O, K) <i>of
the stomach of a ruminant animal, also termed the</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِبَّة</span>, <i>which has</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَطْبَاق</span>: (S, O: [see more in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حفث</span>:]) pl. of the former <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْحَاثٌ</span>. (O, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلَا أَفْحَاثَهُ</span> meaning <i>He filled his</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَوْف</span> [i. e. <i>belly</i>]. (IF, O.)

